# Worker reasoning effort (Chase lock 2026-08-24)

When launching Opus / Fable / Grok via `claude-human-stream` /
`agent-human-stream`, pass `--effort` from the **job lane**, not vibes.

| Lane | Opus | Fable | Grok |
|------|------|-------|------|
| **Code** (implement, PR, land, deploy, RCA that edits) | `medium` | `high` | `xhigh` |
| **Research** (조사, open-source scan, no code change) | `low` | `low` | `medium` |

**Default research owner is Grok.** Opus/Fable research only when Chase
names them — still `low`.

Grok CLI enum is `xhigh|high|medium|low` (not `mid`). The wrapper maps
alias `mid` → `medium` for `--backend grok` only.

Wrapper default when `--effort` is omitted = **code lane**
(Opus `medium`, Fable `high`, Grok `xhigh`). Research launches **must**
pass `--effort` (`medium` for Grok, `low` for Opus/Fable). Mixed
research-then-implement in one worker → code lane.

